---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy – Room Planner';
const description =
  'How Room Planner handles your data: room calculations run locally, layouts are stored in your own browser, no account is required, and imported files never leave your device.';
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/privacy">
  <section class="rp-container py-12">
    <div class="rp-prose">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Room Planner is a tool that runs in your browser. Creating a room, arranging furniture and
        calculating areas all happen on your own device. There is no account, and you do not need to give
        us any personal information to use the planner.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the planner, your current layout is saved automatically in your browser's local
        storage so that you can close the tab and come back to it. If you use <strong>Save</strong>, named
        layouts are stored in the same place.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Saved layouts live on the device and in the browser you created them in.</li>
        <li>They are not uploaded, and we cannot see them.</li>
        <li>Clearing your browser's site data deletes them permanently.</li>
        <li>You can delete any saved layout yourself from the Saved layouts panel.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A layout contains only what you put in it: room dimensions, item names and positions, colors, and
        your view settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Files you import and export</h2>
      <p>
        Exporting a layout creates a file on your device. Importing one reads a file you select and
        processes it in the browser. Imported files are validated before use and are never sent anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2>Images, printing and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        PNG and SVG exports are generated in your browser. If you use <strong>Share</strong>, your device's
        own sharing feature takes over, and where the image goes next is decided by you and the app you
        share it with.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site includes a small, non-identifying event abstraction so that usage can be measured if an
        analytics provider is added in future. Today, no analytics provider is connected and no analytics
        requests are sent. If one is added, this page will be updated to name it and describe what it
        collects before it goes live.
      </p>
      <p>
        We intend to fund Room Planner with advertising. Advertising slots are reserved in the layout but
        no ad network is loaded at present. If Google AdSense or another network is enabled later, this
        page will be updated to say so, and third-party advertising cookies and their purposes will be
        disclosed here along with the relevant opt-out information. Advertising will never be placed over
        the room canvas or next to the editing controls.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        Like any website, requests for the pages, styles and scripts reach the server or content delivery
        network that hosts this site, which may keep standard technical logs such as IP address, browser
        user agent and the page requested. That is a property of how the web works rather than something
        this application does with your layouts.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Room Planner is a general-purpose tool and is not directed at children. It does not ask for or
        knowingly collect personal information from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Delete individual layouts from the Saved layouts panel.</li>
        <li>Clear site data in your browser to remove everything Room Planner has stored.</li>
        <li>Use private browsing if you would rather nothing persists at all.</li>
        <li>Export a layout file if you want a copy you control outside the browser.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If something on this page is unclear, or you think Room Planner is behaving differently from what
        is described here, please get in touch through the contact route listed on the site you obtained
        this application from.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
